   <property name="text">
    <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here is the mashing stage in which the grist is combined with hot water in a mashing tun. This allows the enzymes in the grist to further break down the starches into fermentable sugars. Just like in the milling stage, the varability of the mashing greatly affects the final beer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The tempurature range for the water is 140-158 degrees fahrenheit. Water on the lower end of the spectrum results in a light dry beer, while tempuratures on the higher end of the spectrum result in sweeter beers. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;After the mashing process has concluded, the resulting liquid is called wort.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
   </property>
